# House-price ML pipeline

This project was generated in two steps:

```bash
copier copy <template-source>/templates/python-project <dest> --data package_name={{ package_name }}
copier copy <template-source>/templates/ml <dest>/{{ package_name }} --trust
```

The second step adds a local-only house-price estimator, training task, and
FastAPI serving app on top of the base project. No cloud credentials or
network access are required at any point: training data is bundled at
`resources/house_price_raw.csv`, and the trained model is a local file.

## Train the model

```bash
uv run python -m {{ package_name }}.tasks.train_model
```

Reads `resources/house_price_raw.csv`, fits `HousePredictionModel`, logs the
held-out RMSE/R2, and writes `models/model.pkl`. `models/` is not tracked in
git by default — add `models/` to `.gitignore` if you don't want the trained
artifact committed, or keep it if you'd rather ship a pinned model with the
repo.

## Run the webapp locally

The webapp requires `models/model.pkl` to already exist (see above).

```bash
uv run uvicorn webapp.app:app --reload
```

Then:

```bash
curl localhost:8000/health
curl -X POST localhost:8000/predict -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{
  "instances": [
    {"med_inc": 8.3, "house_age": 41, "ave_rooms": 6.9, "ave_bedrms": 1.0,
     "population": 322, "ave_occup": 2.5, "latitude": 37.88, "longitude": -122.23}
  ]
}'
```

## Build and run the Docker image

Train the model first (`models/model.pkl` must exist in the build context),
then build from the project root:

```bash
uv run python -m {{ package_name }}.tasks.train_model
docker build -f docker/Dockerfile -t {{ package_name }} .
docker run -p 8080:8080 {{ package_name }}
```

## Swapping in a real dataset

`resources/house_price_raw.csv` is a downsampled `sklearn.datasets.fetch_california_housing`
sample, meant as a working placeholder. To use your own data, replace that
file with a CSV containing the same columns (`MedInc`, `HouseAge`, `AveRooms`,
`AveBedrms`, `Population`, `AveOccup`, `Latitude`, `Longitude`,
`MedHouseVal`), or edit `{{ package_name }}/tasks/train_model.py`'s
`frame_to_features` and `TARGET_COLUMN` to match your own schema.
